  "exact_result": "For the raw local smooth-coefficient weak Grushin PDE with c>0 and strict interior rectangular boxes, one actual mixed weak derivative family F is chosen before all finite orders and radii. For every r and nonnegative s, the profile N_r(s) is the finite maximum over exact derivative cost at most r of the sum of 498 actual weighted restricted L2 norms on the shrinking box. Each weighted field is proved MemLp; N is nonnegative, increases with r, and decreases as the box shrinks. On a fixed box and maximum r, one L2 representative family realizes the exact outer norms and satisfies every lower q<=r profile bound. Unweighted shifted derivatives are also represented, including the exact lower-profile domination used by R17.",
  "mathematical_change": "Previously supplied scalar profiles and shifted representative budgets now have an explicit construction from actual local weak derivatives; bounded polynomial weights and the exact r+2 total-order bound discharge all finiteness premises.",
